   217	
   218	### 3.1 First field — what happens to the target
   219	
   220	| Verdict | Meaning |
   221	|---|---|
   222	| `DELIVER` | write the framework's version; the target had nothing |
   223	| `REFRESH` | replace existing content, **backup first** |
   224	| `PRESERVE_OWNED` | do not touch the target; **keep** the delivery record |
   225	| `PRESERVE_UNOWNED` | do not touch the target; do **not** record (the adopter owns it) |
   226	| `OMIT_RECORD` | target stays; its record leaves the manifest |
   227	| `ABORT_SURFACE` | refuse this surface, rc 0, named warning; the run continues |
   228	
   229	`ABORT_SURFACE` is distinct from `PRESERVE_UNOWNED`: it is the outcome when
   230	the framework *wanted* to act and could not do so safely — a failed backup,
