- Tree comparison is file-content-only. `_walk` omits directories and directory symlinks, while `open`/`stat` follow file symlinks. An upgrade can therefore create an out-of-`.claude` empty directory in user mode, or replace a copied file with a symlink to identical bytes, and still pass. [_parity_classify.py:201](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/tests/_parity_classify.py:201), [_parity_classify.py:218](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/tests/_parity_classify.py:218)

- The nightly “full table” authority is derived from the same mutable TSV that drives the run. Deleting any GREEN row shrinks both expected and observed ID sets; the unchanged three REDs and `rc=1` still pass. The committed baseline map is not consulted. [ownership-nightly-gate.sh:76](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/tests/ownership-nightly-gate.sh:76)

- The mtime rider uses whole-second timestamps. A byte-identical refresh occurring in the same second as fixture setup is indistinguishable from preservation, so regressions such as ignoring `--skip` can remain GREEN. The self-check avoids this race by artificially separating timestamps by one minute and therefore does not validate real observation resolution. [test-ownership-table.sh:166](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/tests/test-ownership-table.sh:166), [test-ownership-table.sh:461](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/tests/test-ownership-table.sh:461), [test-ownership-table.sh:741](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/tests/test-ownership-table.sh:741)

P2 findings:

- The user-ceremony transition required by three ownership cells ignores failure, allowing protocol rows to exercise maintainer behavior while reporting GREEN. [test-ownership-table.sh:634](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/tests/test-ownership-table.sh:634)

- The standalone ownership harness exits zero when `AMBIG>0`, contrary to its documented “every row matched” exit contract. The nightly wrapper catches this, but direct release/operator use fails open. [test-ownership-table.sh:696](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/tests/test-ownership-table.sh:696), [test-ownership-table.sh:798](/private/var/folders/9n/hm9srl0s1nz45_p12tj61pd80000gn/T/repass-r2.nPXKYg/wt/scripts/tests/test-ownership-table.sh:798)

Justification: Shell syntax, Python parsing, and the committed 65-row/62-green/3-red counts are internally consistent, and the described model-ledger bump raises no independent b/5 concern. However, the parity and ownership gates can certify concrete deletion, structural-delivery, and coverage regressions, so this payload cannot safely gate rc.2.

VERDICT: NEEDS-CHANGES
